Feature: Data Validation and Processing for Sample Sales Data

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the sample sales data is available in "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"
    And the sample users data is available in "purgo_playground.sample_users_data"

  Scenario: Validate data format and integrity
    Given the data is loaded from "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"
    When the data is checked for format compliance
    Then each "country_cd" should be a non-empty string
    And each "product_id" should be a non-empty string
    And each "qty_sold" should be a positive integer
    And each "sales_date" should be in "YYYY-MM-DD" format

  Scenario: Validate data against business rules
    Given the data is loaded from "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"
    When the data is validated against business rules
    Then the "qty_sold" should not exceed 100 for any record
    And the "sales_date" should not be a future date

  Scenario Outline: Validate data consistency between sales and users data
    Given the data is loaded from "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"
    And the data is loaded from "purgo_playground.sample_users_data"
    When the data is compared for consistency
    Then the "country_cd" in sales data should match "country_cd" in users data
    And the "product_id" in sales data should match "product_id" in users data
    And the "qty_sold" in sales data should match "qty_sold" in users data
    And the "sales_date" in sales data should match "sales_date" in users data
    And the "valid" field in users data should be 1

    Examples:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17  |

  Scenario: Handle missing or invalid data
    Given the data is loaded from "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"
    When the data contains missing or invalid entries
    Then an error message "Data validation failed: Missing or invalid entries found" should be logged
    And the invalid records should be flagged for review

  Scenario: Process valid data for reporting
    Given the data is validated and marked as valid
    When the data is processed for reporting
    Then a summary report should be generated with total "qty_sold" per "country_cd"
    And the report should be stored in "purgo_playground.reports"

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for data processing
    Given the data is loaded from "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"
    When an error occurs during data processing
    Then an error message "<error_message>" should be logged
    And the process should be halted

    Examples:
      | error_message                              |
      | "Database connection error"                |
      | "Data format mismatch error"               |
      | "Insufficient permissions to access table" |